WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.133
I'm Steve Higgins, and we are
about to play "Pup Quiz"!

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.734
-"Pup Quiz"!

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:17.067
-Playing tonight, we have
the host of the "Tonight Show,"

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.133
Mr. Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.133
-Oh, hi, everyone.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:24.267
-And his opponent,
the author of the new cookbook

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:27.133
"Cravings: All together,"
Chrissy Teigen!

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.934
Oh, my gosh!
What a crazy game.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.133
Now, you know, for Halloween,

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.968
all our puppies are
dressed up in costumes.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.300
-Oh, my gosh!

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.067
-This one is dress as a dead --
oh, skeleton.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.367
It's a skeleton.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:43.200
It's Gary Frick Jr.
You know him. You love him.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.267
Here's how the game works.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.634
-Aww, he's cute.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:48.000
-We'll be asking both of you
trivia questions.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.467
Aww! If you answer
the question correctly,

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.467
you win
a golden-retriever puppy.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:53.501
-Oh!

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:54.968
-If you answer it incorrectly,

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.834
your opponent gets the puppy.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.901
Now, most puppies
at the end of the game wins.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.400
-Okay.
-Chrissy, you are up first.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.801
You ready?
-These stakes are so high.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.501
-I know.
I want to win this so bad.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.601
I got to get the little
skeleton puppy.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.767
-What is the technical name for
a group of bats?

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.601
Is it, "A," a haunt,

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.501
"B," a cauldron,

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:17.033
or, "C," a party?

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:19.000
-What?!
-Yeah.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.767
-Can I get help?

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.133
-If you want to give her
the puppy, sure.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.834
-No, I don't. I want the puppy.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.467
It's definitely "C."

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.901
-A party of bats.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:33.167
-I think it's a haunt.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.567
-You think it's a haunt?
Is that your final answer?

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.968
-Yes.
-Ooh, no!

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.501
[ Buzzer ]
It's a cauldron!

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:39.033
-Oh!
-Oh!

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.400
-Wait. I thought it
was a haunt, as well, but --

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.534
-You get Gary Frick Jr.
-Hi, friend!

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.467
-There you go.
-Hi!

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.567
-Oh, my gosh!

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.334
-Hi, buddy.
-I'm so jealous.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.934
-He smells like --
-He smells like strawberries.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.634
-He smells like a puppy!
-They're in costumes, too!

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.767
-Oh, no, he's so cute.
Hi, buddy.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.434
-Alright, Jimmy,
next question is for you.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:01:59.834
-Yeah. Love it.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:03.033
-In your favorite movie,
the 1985 movie "Teen Wolf,"

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:05.868
Michael J. Fox's
basketball team have what

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.834
animal as their mascot?

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:10.133
-Wolf?
-No.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.467
-Dragon?

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.534
-Maybe.
-Or Beaver?

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:14.634
-It can't be a wolf.
He is a wolf.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.968
-Right. Teen Wolf.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.334
-Dragon doesn't really --
I don't associate dragon with

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.701
a high-school team name.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.701
Like, the basketball team,
"We're the dragons."

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.167
-Right.
-So I think the Beavers.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.434
I think "C."
-Final answer?

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:26.834
-I think it's Beaver, too.
-I think it's Beaver.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.334
[ Ding ]
-Beaver -- that is correct!

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.334
Oh, my gosh!

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:35.067
Jimmy getting the role of
a puppuccino.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.300
This is a Frappuccino
made of puppy skull.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.667
-What is this?

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:43.767
-Mary Kennedy as a puppuccino.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:48.267
Not a Frappuccino.
A puppuccino.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.501
-Aww!

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.133
-It gets better when
there's more of them.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.567
-It's so cute.

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:56.667
They are so cute.
[ Dog barking ]

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:57.968
-You know what that sound means.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.501
-No.
-Time for "Double Puppardy."

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:00.601
-What does that mean?

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.767
-Questions are now worth
two puppies!

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:05.067
-Okay, don't scare the puppies.
-Okay.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:07.067
Ghost sharks.
We all love ghost sharks, sure.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.400
-I don't even know
what that means.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.067
-They have a retractable
sex organ called a "clasper" --

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:16.701
ouch -- that comes out of what
part of their body?

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:21.133
The tail, the forehead,
or the dorsal fin?

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.400
The clasper.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.434
-Mm, it's "Double Puppardy."
-Yep, "Double Puppardy."

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.334
-Forehead?
-Is that your final answer?

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:28.434
-Yes!

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:29.601
-Forehead! You are right!
[ Ding ]

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.334
Oh, my gosh!

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.167
-Oh, no!
-A brontosaurus and a chef.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.968
-Oh, no. Oh, no.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:41.601
-Please welcome Lisa Armstrong
and Peter Winston.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:44.400
Peter loves cooking,
just like you.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.634
-Oh, no!

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:47.767
Oh, no!
-Oh, there you go.

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.901
Oh, look at that
little brontosaur.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:51.734
-I'm gonna cry.
-Okay, Jimmy.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.868
Okay, Jimmy, how many different
species of spiders are there?

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.400
-Oh, easy. I don't even need
the multiple choice.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.133
-Oh, really? Then what is it?

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:01.801
-Just show it for fun.
-Okay, just for the people.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:02.801
-Just for the audience.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:08.801
-450, 4,500, or 45,000 spiders?

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:12.167
[ Laughter ]
-We're so happy right now.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.167
-It's the best game.
I don't want it to end.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:15.634
Well, I think there's
a lot of spiders, right?

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.234
-You think there's a lot
of spiders?

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:20.367
-I'm going to say "C,"
45,000 spiders.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:21.434
-That is correct!
[ Ding ]

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:28.901
Now, your puppies are dressed as
Frankenpup and a rodeo horse.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:33.334
Say hello to Kyle McAdams
and Michelle Gordon,

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.701
the rodeo horse.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.567
-Hi, bud. Ooh! Yeah, sure.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:38.868
Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:39.934
[ Dog barking ]

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.501
-Oh, you know
what that sound means.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:42.801
Time for "Final Puppardy."
Yep.

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:43.801
-Oh.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:46.133
-For all of
your opponent's puppies.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:47.467
[ Both gasp ]

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:51.033
So, pick up the iPads.
This is a numerical one.

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:53.234
-Alright, gotcha.
So this is a numeric --

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:54.267
-Numeric answer.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.701
Whoever's the closest,
up or down,

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.100
gets all the puppies.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.634
-Yep, gotcha. Okay.
-Ready?

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:01.767
-Yep, hold on. Rodeo pup...

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.801
-How many pounds --
-I think I'm missing a puppy.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:06.300
Sorry.
I lost one of the puppies.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.100
-Oh, no.
-Oh, where's the skeleton puppy?

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.100
Oh, here he is.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.100
-There he is. There's skeleton.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.667
That's Gary Frick Jr.
-No, of course it is.

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.901
-How many pounds does
the world's largest

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:18.267
salamander weigh?

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:19.834
World's largest salamander.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.467
You have 10 seconds, starting...

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:22.567
-What do you mean 10 seconds?

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:23.934
-...now!
-Oh, my God!

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:27.334
-9, 8, 7...

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:28.467
-You're scaring the pups.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:29.934
-Wait. Without going over?
-You can go over.

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.901
It doesn't matter.
-Okay.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.033
-World's largest salamander.
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.400
Okay.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.567
Jimmy, what was your answer?

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:38.667
You wrote the word "So."

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.601
-No, it should be 50.

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.467
-Oh, 50. 50. Of course. 50.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:43.934
50 or so.

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:45.501
-50 pounds.
-50 pounds.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.601
-50-or-so-pound salamander?

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.601
-20. 20 pounds.
-20 pounds.

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:50.801
The winner is Jimmy!
[ Dinging ]

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:53.701
-No!
-130 pounds!

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:55.100
Oh, my gosh!

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.400
-Chrissy, I'm gonna let you
win this one,

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.534
just 'cause it's Halloween.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.901
Why not?
Come on. This is so good.

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:02.868
Get these puppies.
-There you go.

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:07.868
-Thank you. Hi!
This is this the best game!

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:09.834
All the puppies!

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:13.200
-There you go.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.834
-I love it!
-Look at these.

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:18.801
Look at all the puppies.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.400
-Our thanks to Chrissy Teigen
and all these adorable puppies.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.267
Stick around for more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:24.934
Happy Halloween!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.400
Hi, guys!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.400
♪♪

